  "reason": "Evidence: scvi_n200 dramatically outperforms scgpt (0.725 vs 0.520) in the best multimodal setup (imagenet_vit_l + transformer), and weighted fusion edges out concat. The current best (config_012, 0.725) uses scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + transformer + weighted. Question: We have not yet tested pca_n2000 in this top multimodal configuration. config_030 (pca_n2000, imagenet_vit_l, transformer, weighted) is a clean single-variable comparison against config_012, isolating the RNA encoder effect in the best overall architecture. Why this is the best next experiment: With only 2 experiments remaining, I need to know whether the RNA encoder choice is truly saturated at scvi_n200 or whether pca_n2000 could be competitive in the strongest multimodal setup. If pca_n2000 is close to 0.725, it opens a new direction for the final experiments; if it falls well below, it confirms scvi_n200 is essential and I can dedicate the last 2 experiments to fine-tuning around the scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + transformer + weighted core (e.g., testing singleprofile or alternative fusion). This maximally reduces uncertainty about the most impactful design axis before the budget closes."
}

